sec.p:
The dynamic model tracks three sets of variables: (1) Microbial biomass concentration Mi for each species i = 1,2, …, Nspe ; (2) concentrations of each siderophore type Rj (j = 1,2,…, Nsid); (3) Free iron concentration Riron:
(1)
dMidt=Mi⋅(γ⋅αi0⋅∑jvij⋅Jj−d)+σ,wherei=1,⋯,Nspe. \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{gathered} \frac{d M_i}{d t}=M_i \cdot\left(\gamma \cdot \alpha_{i 0} \cdot \sum_j v_{i j} \cdot J_j-d\right)+\sigma, \\ \text { where } i=1, \cdots, N_{\mathrm{spe}} . \end{gathered}$$\end{document}
(2)
dRjdt=∑iMi⋅αij⋅ϵj−d⋅Rj,wherej=1,⋯,Nsid. \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d R_{j}}{d t}=\sum_{i} M_{i} \cdot \alpha_{i j} \cdot \epsilon_{j}-d \cdot R_{j}, \text { where } j=1, \cdots, N_{\text {sid }} \text {. } \tag{2} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
(3)
dRirondt=d⋅(Rsupply−Riron)−∑i,jMi⋅vij⋅Jj. \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d R_{\mathrm{iron}}}{d t}=d \cdot\left(R_{\mathrm{supply}}-R_{\mathrm{iron}}\right)-\sum_{i, j} M_{i} \cdot v_{i j} \cdot J_{j} . \tag{3} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
Varying parameters α and v generates a continuum of strategies, from “pure-producers” (exclusively utilizing their own siderophores) to “pure-cheaters” (no production) and “partial producers” (producing one siderophore while exploiting several other types) (Fig. 1B).
